---
import "../../styles/global.css";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head><!-- Start cookieyes banner --> <script id="cookieyes" type="text/javascript" src="https://cdn-cookieyes.com/client_data/e9c032e34948c08e8ad6b9973971db36/script.js"></script> <!-- End cookieyes banner -->
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />

    <link
      rel="icon"
      type="image/png"
      href="/images/kasodi-favicon.png"
    />

    <title>The Art of Quiet Luxury | KASODI</title>

    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Discover the art of quiet luxury through natural materials, thoughtful craftsmanship, restrained colour and beautiful objects chosen to last."
    />
  </head>

  <body>

    <Header />

    <main class="journal-story-page">

      <!-- BREADCRUMB -->

      <div class="product-breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span>·</span>
        <a href="/#journal">Journal</a>
        <span>·</span>
        <span>The Art of Quiet Luxury</span>
      </div>


      <!-- HERO -->

      <section class="journal-story-hero">

        <p class="product-detail-eyebrow">
          INTERIORS & STYLE
        </p>

        <h1>
          The Art of<br />
          Quiet Luxury
        </h1>

        <p class="journal-story-intro">
          Quiet luxury is less about what a home costs and more about how it feels —
          considered, comfortable and filled with things chosen with intention.
        </p>

      </section>


      <!-- HERO IMAGE -->

      <section class="journal-story-cover">

            <img
             src="/images/journal/the-art-of-quiet-luxury-hero.png"
              alt="Warm Mediterranean interior with natural materials, botanical details and quiet luxury styling"
             />

        </section>

      <!-- 01 -->

      <section class="journal-story-row journal-story-divider">

        <div class="journal-story-copy">

          <p class="journal-story-number">
            01
          </p>

          <h2>
            Choose materials that feel good
          </h2>

          <p>
            Quiet luxury begins with materials you want to touch. Washed linen,
            warm wood, softly glazed ceramics, woven fibres, stone and textured
            glass bring depth to a room without demanding attention. Their beauty
            comes from subtle variations rather than perfectly polished surfaces.
          </p>

          <p>
            Natural materials also become more interesting with time. Linen
            softens, wood develops character and handmade-looking ceramics reveal
            small irregularities that make each piece feel individual. Instead of
            filling a room with decoration, begin with a few materials that create
            warmth on their own. Often, texture can do more for an interior than
            another decorative object.
          </p>

        </div>


        <div class="journal-story-mood">

  <img
    src="/images/categories/category-home-decor.png"
    alt="Warm home decor with natural materials and softly layered textures"
  />

</div>
</section>


      <!-- 02 -->

      <section class="journal-story-row journal-story-row-product journal-story-divider">

        <div class="journal-inline-product">

          <a href="/kasodi-edit/botanical-vintage-pitcher">
            <img
              src="/images/kasodi-edit/kasodi-edit-floral-ceramic-pitcher.png"
              alt="Botanical vintage pitcher by Ethereal Eves"
            />
          </a>

          <div class="journal-inline-product-info">

            <p class="journal-story-product-category">
              HOME DECOR
            </p>

            <h3>
              Botanical Vintage Pitcher
            </h3>

            <p class="journal-story-product-brand">
              Ethereal Eves
            </p>

            <a
              href="/kasodi-edit/botanical-vintage-pitcher"
              class="journal-story-discover"
            >
              Discover →
            </a>

          </div>

        </div>


        <div class="journal-story-copy">

          <p class="journal-story-number">
            02
          </p>

          <h2>
            Let craftsmanship do the talking
          </h2>

          <p>
            The most memorable objects rarely need to announce themselves. A
            beautifully shaped handle, an embroidered edge, a delicate botanical
            motif or an unusual glaze can give an everyday object presence. These
            are details you may not notice immediately, but they are often what
            makes a piece worth keeping.
          </p>

          <p>
            This is where choosing fewer, more distinctive objects makes a
            difference. A ceramic pitcher can be both useful and decorative, while
            a beautifully finished bowl can sit comfortably on an open shelf even
            when it is empty. Quiet luxury is not about surrounding yourself with
            expensive things. It is about noticing when something has been made
            with care.
          </p>

        </div>

      </section>


      <!-- 03 -->

      <section class="journal-story-row journal-story-row-product-reverse journal-story-divider">

        <div class="journal-story-copy">

          <p class="journal-story-number">
            03
          </p>

          <h2>
            Use colour with restraint
          </h2>

          <p>
            Quiet does not have to mean beige. Deep green glass, dusty blue
            ceramics, muted ochre, warm ivory and soft tobacco tones can bring
            personality into a room while still feeling sophisticated and calm.
          </p>

          <p>
            The key is repetition rather than abundance. Choose one or two colours
            and allow them to appear gently throughout the space — perhaps in a
            glass, a cushion, a painted detail or a piece of pottery. Against
            natural materials and a calm background, even a small amount of colour
            becomes more expressive. A single green glass catching afternoon light
            can sometimes contribute more to a room than an entire collection of
            matching accessories.
          </p>

        </div>


        <div class="journal-inline-product">

          <a href="/kasodi-edit/boston-green-wine-glass">
            <img
              src="/images/kasodi-edit/kasodi-edit-villeroy-boch-boston-green-glass.png"
              alt="Boston green wine glass by Villeroy and Boch"
            />
          </a>

          <div class="journal-inline-product-info">

            <p class="journal-story-product-category">
              GLASSWARE
            </p>

            <h3>
              Boston Green Wine Glass
            </h3>

            <p class="journal-story-product-brand">
              Villeroy & Boch
            </p>

            <a
              href="/kasodi-edit/boston-green-wine-glass"
              class="journal-story-discover"
            >
              Discover →
            </a>

          </div>

        </div>

      </section>


      <!-- 04 -->

      <section class="journal-story-row journal-story-row-product journal-story-divider">

        <div class="journal-inline-product">

          <a href="/new-finds/vintage-butterfly-photo-frame">
            <img
              src="/images/new-finds/vintage-butterfly-photo-frame.png"
              alt="Vintage butterfly photo frame by LEYI DECOR"
            />
          </a>

          <div class="journal-inline-product-info">

            <p class="journal-story-product-category">
              DECORATIVE OBJECTS
            </p>

            <h3>
              Vintage Butterfly Photo Frame
            </h3>

            <p class="journal-story-product-brand">
              LEYI DECOR
            </p>

            <a
              href="/new-finds/vintage-butterfly-photo-frame"
              class="journal-story-discover"
            >
              Discover →
            </a>

          </div>

        </div>


        <div class="journal-story-copy">

          <p class="journal-story-number">
            04
          </p>

          <h2>
            Mix old and new
          </h2>

          <p>
            Rooms with character rarely look as though everything arrived on the
            same day. A vintage-inspired frame beside a contemporary object, an
            aged wooden surface beneath modern ceramics or a botanical piece placed
            on a simple console creates a sense of history and makes an interior
            feel more personal.
          </p>

          <p>
            The goal is not to recreate a particular period. It is to avoid making
            a home feel overly coordinated. Allow different finishes, shapes and
            influences to coexist. When there is a common thread of colour,
            material or mood, pieces from different styles can feel surprisingly
            natural together. A home becomes more interesting when it looks
            collected over time.
          </p>

        </div>

      </section>


      <!-- 05 + NOTE -->

      <section class="journal-story-closing">

        <div class="journal-story-ending">

          <p class="journal-story-number">
            05
          </p>

          <h2>
            Make comfort part of the design
          </h2>

          <p>
            A beautiful room should invite you to use it. Cushions should be
            comfortable enough to lean against, throws should be within reach and
            lighting should become softer in the evening. Linen does not need to
            remain perfectly pressed. These small signs of everyday life prevent
            an elegant interior from becoming too formal.
          </p>

          <p>
            Layer embroidered or patterned cushions with quieter textiles, add a
            throw to the arm of a chair and let curtains move with the breeze
            rather than arranging everything perfectly. Comfort is not separate
            from good design. In the most successful rooms, it is part of what
            makes the space beautiful.
          </p>

        </div>


        <aside class="journal-story-note">

          <p class="product-detail-eyebrow">
            KASODI NOTE
          </p>

          <h3>
            A room does not need to prove that it is luxurious. It simply needs
            to feel considered, comfortable and personal.
          </h3>

        </aside>

      </section>


      <!-- PIECES FOR THE LOOK -->

      <section class="journal-look-edit">

        <div class="journal-look-heading">

          <p class="product-detail-eyebrow">
            KASODI EDIT
          </p>

          <h2>
            Pieces for the Look
          </h2>

          <p>
            Three thoughtful finds that bring texture, colour and quiet character
            to a collected interior.
          </p>

        </div>


        <div class="journal-look-grid">


          <article class="journal-look-card">

            <a
              href="/kasodi-edit/botanical-vintage-pitcher"
              class="journal-look-image"
            >
              <img
                src="/images/kasodi-edit/kasodi-edit-floral-ceramic-pitcher.png"
                alt="Botanical vintage pitcher by Ethereal Eves"
              />
            </a>

            <div class="journal-look-info">

              <p class="journal-story-product-category">
                HOME DECOR
              </p>

              <h3>
                Botanical Vintage Pitcher
              </h3>

              <p class="journal-story-product-brand">
                Ethereal Eves
              </p>

              <a
                href="/kasodi-edit/botanical-vintage-pitcher"
                class="journal-story-discover"
              >
                Discover →
              </a>

            </div>

          </article>


          <article class="journal-look-card">

            <a
              href="/kasodi-edit/boston-green-wine-glass"
              class="journal-look-image"
            >
              <img
                src="/images/kasodi-edit/kasodi-edit-villeroy-boch-boston-green-glass.png"
                alt="Boston green wine glass by Villeroy and Boch"
              />
            </a>

            <div class="journal-look-info">

              <p class="journal-story-product-category">
                GLASSWARE
              </p>

              <h3>
                Boston Green Wine Glass
              </h3>

              <p class="journal-story-product-brand">
                Villeroy & Boch
              </p>

              <a
                href="/kasodi-edit/boston-green-wine-glass"
                class="journal-story-discover"
              >
                Discover →
              </a>

            </div>

          </article>


          <article class="journal-look-card">

            <a
              href="/kasodi-edit/embroidered-garden-cushions"
              class="journal-look-image"
            >
              <img
                src="/images/kasodi-edit/kasodi-edit-embroidered-green-cushions.png"
                alt="Embroidered garden cushions by Running Elephant"
              />
            </a>

            <div class="journal-look-info">

              <p class="journal-story-product-category">
                TEXTILES
              </p>

              <h3>
                Embroidered Garden Cushions
              </h3>

              <p class="journal-story-product-brand">
                Running Elephant
              </p>

              <a
                href="/kasodi-edit/embroidered-garden-cushions"
                class="journal-story-discover"
              >
                Discover →
              </a>

            </div>

          </article>


        </div>

      </section>


      <!-- FINAL -->

      <section class="journal-article-final">

        <p class="product-detail-eyebrow">
          THE KASODI APPROACH
        </p>

        <h2>
          Choose fewer things,<br />
          but choose them with attention.
        </h2>

        <p>
          Look for beautiful materials, thoughtful details and objects that can
          remain part of your home long after a trend has passed.
        </p>

      </section>

    </main>

    <Footer />

  </body>
</html>